{"agent":"fix-import-state","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The exclusion in `done_counts` keys entirely off `ev.data.get(\"imported\")`, but nothing in this change (and nothing in the import path it touches) produces that key, and the new regression test fabricates it by hand (`{\"kind\": \"phase\", \"imported\": True}`), so the test cannot fail when the producer does not stamp it. If the importer appends the historical `item.completed` events verbatim — the normal event-sourced-import behaviour, and the reading implied by the operator's alternative \"baseline each cadence at import time (count only items completed after the import)\" — then `st.imported_done` stays empty, `done_counts` still returns `(3713, 480)`, and `ddflow complete 1` is still refused with \"periodic pass overdue: architecture_review (480 of 2 phases since the last)\". The change needs either the import to stamp `imported` on each closed item (or emit an import-boundary/baseline event), plus a regression test that drives that real path rather than injecting the flag itself.","digest":"e5a7653ce5408c25","location":"ddflow/core/handlers/items.py:116 (with tests/test_triggers_unified.py:305)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/handlers/items.py:116 (with tests/test_triggers_unified.py:305)"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The imported history this test builds contains no completed phase: `todo.md` is `## P` with `- [x] **P.1**` and `- [ ] **P.2** — open`, so phase `P` stays incomplete and the phase element of the returned pair is `0` both before and after the fix. The bug being closed has two halves — the refusal message quoted in the intent is `periodic pass overdue: architecture_review (480 of 2 phases since the last)` and doctor's `3713 tasks since` — and this test only discriminates on the task counter (unfixed: the imported `P.1` makes it `(0,1)`; fixed: `(0,0)`). A fix that baselines completed tasks at import but leaves the *phase* cadence counting imported phase completions would still make `SV.done_counts(st) == (0, 0)` here (no phase is complete), so the exact \"480 of 2 phases\" symptom would go unguarded and a future regression to it would not turn this test red. To actually pin the reported behaviour the fixture needs at least one phase that the import closes (all its tasks `[x]`, nothing left open) and an assertion that the phase counter is `0`; similarly, asserting the internal `done_counts` helper rather than that a subsequent `ddflow complete` on the imported repo is *accepted* leaves the user-visible failure path (`complete` being refused) untested.","digest":"78e072b10ac2bc32","location":"tests/test_import_verify.py:545 (test_imported_completions_are_not_counted_by_the_cadence_passes)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_import_verify.py:545 (test_imported_completions_are_not_counted_by_the_cadence_passes)"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":1,"delta_from":"df206f5c2329ef0e4671c94651f00d2a94f7e7a7","delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":1498,"diff_sha":"183febc57c790edb59bb2bce4e3854bcd5de58ae069d09c760c1e227fffdbe14","diff_source":"delta review of 1 commit since df206f5c23","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":122.3,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"full_coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"81c9c7e7dd3d464a","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-cadence-counts-imported-history.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261012T134357Z-e05f0f26.jsonl","passed_on_refutation":{"confirmed":1,"max_rounds":2,"refuted":1,"rounds":2},"reason":"","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"64cfc44c97fc5837c1c7df5ac79c0d91850362d6","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/core/handlers/items.py:116 (with tests/test_triggers_unified.py:305)","tests/test